{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Handoff (session rebar-session-3d705fec, 2026-11-17 PST, origin/main 83ca81e709e). Not claimed, no code changed.\n\n### Established\n- REB-6995 is gone. Read-only checks: `search_issues('key = \"REB-6995\"')` returns `[]`, and ACLI `workitem search` answers \"issue does not exist\". This agrees with the run's missing `leaked.log`.\n- The default-run half of AC 2 already holds on main. `7c3cb5e9a4f` (bug 5f29-9bed-5a47-4a25) marks `test_delete_permission_probe` `@pytest.mark.live` (tests/integration/test_reconcile_live_e2e.py:284), and `make test` and CI run `-m \"integration and not live\"` (Makefile:617). The probe therefore runs only on an explicit `pytest -m live`, and a local `make verify` no longer writes to live Jira.\n- Timed probe at host load 18-30, run alone: 3 rounds of the same create → poll → delete as the test, instrumented per attempt (REB-7248, REB-7249, REB-7250, all deleted). Each issue was visible on the first attempt (summary search 0.36-0.54 s). The key search returned `[]` on that first attempt in 2 of the 3 rounds while the summary search already found the issue. No failure reproduced.\n\n### Not established\n- AC 1, the cause of the recurrence, is open: no timed failing run exists. The original failure happened inside the full live group (`xdist_group(\"live_reconcile_e2e\")`, load 25-40), with other live tests creating and searching issues at the same time.\n- The poll cannot explain its own failures. `_poll_until_visible` and `_issue_exists` (test_reconcile_live_e2e.py:354-419) swallow every search exception as \"not visible\". A failing run therefore cannot tell 120 s of index lag apart from 120 s of rejected searches (for example rate limiting from the concurrent live group).\n\n### Needs a human decision\nReproducing the failure means running the whole `-m live` group repeatedly under load. Every run creates and deletes many REB issues in production Jira. Which way should this go?\n(1) Authorize N full `pytest -m live` runs under load, with the poll changed first to record each attempt's latency and exception text in the assertion message, so the next failure names its cause.\n(2) **Land only the poll instrumentation (test-only, no live runs now), and keep this bug open until the next `-m live` failure supplies the timed evidence.**\n(3) Close as `superseded` by 5f29-9bed-5a47-4a25, accepting that the opt-in-only probe may still flake."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1794940640402629228,"uuid":"126ebf93-819d-4660-b916-2513017e9d99"}